      "id": "mjtehbv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to President"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The President is the head of the Indian State, the first citizen of India, and the supreme commander of the armed forces.",
        "The President is elected indirectly by an Electoral College consisting of elected members of Parliament and State Legislative Assemblies.",
        "Qualifications require being an Indian citizen, at least 35 years of age, and qualified for election as a member of the Lok Sabha.",
        "Powers of the President span Executive, Legislative, Financial, Judicial, and Emergency domains.",
        "The President can be removed from office before term completion through the process of impeachment for 'violation of the Constitution'."
      ],
      "id": "i5xme6n"
    },
